{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.BraidingInducedOrdering","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.BraidingInducedOrdering","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFounded","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Lex","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.braiding_induced_ordering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.braiding_induced_ordering","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L171-L174","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:braiding-induced-ordering","label":"prop:braiding-induced-ordering","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.degLex_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.degLex_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L157-L169","doc":"Full admissibility: DegLex is preserved under concatenation\nwith common prefix and suffix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.degLex_admissible_lex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.degLex_admissible_lex","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L142-L155","doc":"Admissibility (lex component): concatenation with a common\nprefix and a common suffix preserves the lex ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.lex_append_suffix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.lex_append_suffix","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L121-L140","doc":"Appending a common **suffix** preserves `List.Lex`, provided the two\nwords have equal length.\n\nMathlib supplies only the common-*prefix* direction\n(`List.Lex.append_left`); there is no suffix lemma, and the suffix\nstatement is **false** without the length hypothesis: with\n`w = []`, `w' = [0]`, `v = [1]` we have `Lex (· < ·) [] [0]` by\n`Lex.nil`, yet `Lex (· < ·) [1] [0, 1]` fails — the heads `1` and `0`\nare unequal and `1 < 0` is false.  Equal length rules that case out:\nthe `Lex.nil` constructor forces `w = []` and `w' ≠ []`, which\ncontradicts `hlen`.  The remaining two constructors carry the suffix\nthrough unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.degLex_admissible_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.degLex_admissible_length","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L113-L119","doc":"Admissibility (length component): concatenation preserves\nthe length ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.degLex_wellOrdered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.degLex_wellOrdered","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L88-L111","doc":"**DegLex on `List (Fin n)` is well-founded.**\n\nEmbed into `ℕ ×ₗ ℕ` via `w ↦ (w.length, encode w)`. Both components are\n`<` on `ℕ`, so `WellFounded.prod_lex` applies.\n\nThe earlier proof embedded into `ℕ ×ₗ List (Fin n)` and appealed to\nwell-foundedness of `List.Lex` in the second slot. That is **false**\n(see `encode_lt_of_lex`), so the route could not be repaired by fixing a\nname — the second component has to be replaced by something that really\nis well-founded, which is what `encode` provides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.encode_lt_of_lex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.encode_lt_of_lex","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L56-L86","doc":"**At equal length, `List.Lex` is exactly `encode`-order.**\n\nThis is the step the previous proof was missing. It cannot be replaced by\na well-foundedness fact about `List.Lex` itself, because `List.Lex (· < ·)`\non `List (Fin n)` is **not** well-founded for `n ≥ 2`:\n`[0,1] > [0,0,1] > [0,0,0,1] > …` descends forever. Restricting to equal\nlength is what rules those chains out, and `encode` is what converts the\nrestricted relation into `<` on `ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.encode_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.encode_lt","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L40-L54","doc":"A word of length `L` encodes strictly below `n^L` — the carry bound that\nkeeps the leading digit dominant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.encode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.encode","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L31-L38","doc":"Base-`n` positional encoding of a word over `Fin n`:\n`encode [a₀, a₁, …, a_{k-1}] = Σᵢ aᵢ · n^(k-1-i)`.\n\nThis is the arithmetic stand-in for lexicographic comparison **at fixed\nlength**, and it is what makes `degLex_wellOrdered` provable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DegLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DegLex","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-induced-ordering.lean#L24-L29","doc":"The degree-lex relation on `List α`: first compare lengths,\nthen compare lexicographically at equal length. ","signatureChunk":0}]}